1
00:00:00,644 --> 00:00:03,644
One command. A seeded portal. This is the real application.

2
00:00:05,315 --> 00:00:08,715
Organizer control room. The event, its submissions, and judge progress.

3
00:00:10,211 --> 00:00:13,611
Calibration lab: raw and normalized, side by side.

4
00:00:14,957 --> 00:00:18,157
Public gallery. Forty-one fixture projects. No account required.

5
00:00:19,774 --> 00:00:22,574
Search and track filter, server-side.

6
00:00:22,882 --> 00:00:27,082
A participant tries to submit after the deadline. The server refuses: 403 event_closed, naming the fixture's own close date. The form being disabled is a courtesy; this is the enforcement.

7
00:00:27,314 --> 00:00:31,314
Assignment is the authorization unit. A judge sees only assigned projects, in eligible tracks.

8
00:00:32,555 --> 00:00:35,555
Judge desk. Project, rubric, evidence and notes on one surface.

9
00:00:38,281 --> 00:00:41,681
Autosave is debounced and says so. A judge's work is never lost to a refresh.

10
00:00:43,327 --> 00:00:46,727
Reload. The scores come back: 5. Silence here would be data loss.

11
00:00:46,947 --> 00:00:51,147
403 peer_isolation. This is the check the spec weights most heavily, and the refusal carries no score rows in its body.

12
00:00:51,359 --> 00:00:55,559
403 forbidden. A participant is a known user with a valid session, so this is a role check, not a missing login.

13
00:00:55,775 --> 00:00:58,975
The CSV is organizer-only too. The refusal body is not a CSV.

14
00:01:00,746 --> 00:01:05,346
Judge severity spans 2.000 to 4.222 on a 1-5 scale. Raw and normalized are both published, with the movement and a reason for each.

15
00:01:05,574 --> 00:01:09,974
Published in normalized mode. Fingerprint 305adcbf33fe4257 is written to the audit log, so the exact ranking is reproducible.

16
00:01:11,514 --> 00:01:14,514
Every high-value mutation is here — refusals included.

17
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:19,130
Seven of seven. Claimed T1 T2, verified T1 T2. This file is committed unedited.

18
00:01:19,349 --> 00:01:24,349
Self-hosted, offline, judge isolation in the backend, and a scoring model you can argue with.
